ember has come in under 90% of normal in 36 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025 that same pair came in at 48% of normal on the middle, and January to February was at 56% that year. So far in 2026, April to May sits at 67% of normal on the middle. All 6 grids had their driest year in 1965, between 61% and 63% of normal.</p>"}
